schema: source-system
object:
  title: SuperBenefit Knowledge Garden
  type: docs-site
  steward: SuperBenefit
  return_path: >-
    Not stated in the article — it describes the Knowledge Garden as an
    Obsidian vault maintained as Markdown in a public Git repository and
    published with Quartz, which implies a pull-request-style contribution
    path, but no explicit contribute-back channel is named. Needs steward
    confirmation (see companion signal object).
  url: https://knowledge.superbenefit.org/
  what_it_curates: >-
    Docs, a lexicon of defined terms, a curated link library, and design
    patterns for community/DAO practice, maintained as Markdown in a public
    Git repository.
  why_it_matters: >-
    Cited in the article as a working, community-scale example of the
    Markdown + Git + static-publisher pattern: a knowledge commons a small
    team can run for years with no platform bill and full ownership of the
    archive.
  how_to_credit: SuperBenefit
